@startuml k_checkout
!include _style.puml
title K — the owner's scenario: choose seats, keep them 40 minutes, pay

participant "Buyer A" as A
participant "Database" as DB
participant "Buyer B" as B

A -> DB : hold seats 3,4 — expires in 40 minutes
... A browses, compares, comes back at minute 39 ...
A -> DB : pre-payment check: still held? → true (identical in every design)
activate A
note over A : paying… the card takes 2 minutes

alt K1 — payment window
  A -> DB : minute 39: begin checkout → expires_at := max(expires_at, now + 10 min), once
  B -> DB : minute 40.5: tries seats 3,4 → still held
  A -> DB : minute 41: confirm → **sold**
else S1 — checked confirmation
  B -> DB : minute 40.5: takes seats 3,4 (A's hold has expired)
  A -> DB : minute 41: UPDATE … WHERE hold = A AND held AND expires_at > now() → 0 rows
  DB --> A : **refused after paying**: refund. No double sale — but the promise was broken at its edge.
else K0 — naive confirmation (NEGATIVE CONTROL)
  B -> DB : minute 40.5: takes seats 3,4
  A -> DB : minute 41: UPDATE … SET sold to A WHERE seat IN (3,4)
  DB --> A : 2 rows — **a sale after expiry, over B's hold**
end
deactivate A
@enduml
